  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Erection of a two storey detached dwelling in rear garden with access from Palmerston Road and provision of cycle and refuse stores and associated landscaping and boundary treatment.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of excessive footprint, limited plot size and siting, would constitute as an overdevelopment of the site. It would fail to respect the prevailing character of the surrounding area would not be of a scale suitable to the function of the location contrary to Policies 7 and 9 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The proposed development, by reasons of its location on a constrained site and poor design quality appears as an incompatible development which is out of context with the surrounding development. As such, the proposal is unacceptable in design terms, contrary to the principles of sustainable development of the National Planning Policy Framework, Policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan 2021, Policies 28 and 30 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018, and the Council's adopted Supplementary Planning Document 14: Creating Locally Distinctive Places.",
    "The proposed dwelling due to the siting, scale and proximity to the site boundaries would result in a detrimental impact on the amenities of the occupants of 9, 11 and 13 William Road in terms of outlook and visual intrusion.  The proposed dwellinghouse is therefore contrary to Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Without evidence to the contrary, it is considered that the proposal would place unacceptable pressure on the on-street parking situation at the site by reason of the absence of a completed S106 legal agreement to secure the prohibition of the future occupiers from obtaining residents car parking permits. As such, the application would be contrary to Policy T6.1 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy 37 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
